  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a grid containing fresh oranges, rotten oranges, and empty cells, find the minimum time required for all fresh oranges to become rotten. Each rotten orange can rot its adjacent fresh oranges (up, down, left, right) in one second.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - the number of test cases\nFor each test case:\n\nFirst line contains two integers NNN and MMM - dimensions of the grid\nNext NNN lines each contain MMM integers - the grid values\n\n\n\n0: Empty cell \n\n1: Fresh orange \n\n2: Rotten orange\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case:\n\nPrint minimum time required to rot all oranges\nPrint -1 if it's impossible to rot all oranges",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
